/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# insta pending snapshots
**/*.snap.new
**/*.pending-snap

# Compiled Jairs output
/examples/**/*.o
/examples/**/*.dSYM
/tests/**/*.o
/out
/*.o

# tree-sitter artefacts.
#
# `src/scanner.c` is hand-written — nested block comments cannot be expressed as a token
# regex — so it is tracked.
#
# **`src/parser.c` and the headers beside it are generated and NOW TRACKED**, which reverses
# ADR-0025 §3 (see ADR-0199 §10). That section rejected committing them because "all
# generated output is regenerated by the gate", and the premise expired: Zed builds a grammar
# by cloning the repository at a revision and running `clang` over `src/parser.c` directly —
# it never runs `tree-sitter generate`, so a repository without the generated parser cannot
# supply a grammar to it at all.
#
# Tracking them also *strengthens* gate 6 rather than weakening it. That gate regenerates and
# then checks `git status` for drift; while these were ignored, drift could never be reported
# for them, so a `grammar.js` change with a stale parser beside it was invisible. Now the
# artefact an editor consumes cannot silently disagree with the grammar it came from.
#
# `grammar.json` and `node-types.json` stay ignored: nothing reads them here, and they would
# be pure churn on every regeneration.
/tree-sitter-jairs/src/grammar.json
/tree-sitter-jairs/src/node-types.json
/tree-sitter-jairs/build/
/tree-sitter-jairs/node_modules/
/tree-sitter-jairs/*.wasm

# The Zed extension's WASM build. Zed compiles the extension itself from source when it is
# installed, so a checked-in artefact would be stale immediately and is never read.
/editors/zed/target/
/editors/zed/*.wasm
/editors/zed/Cargo.lock

.DS_Store

# The tree-sitter parser Neovim loads, built by editors/nvim/build.sh from the
# git-ignored generated parser.c. Regenerate rather than commit a binary.
/editors/nvim/parser/*.so

# A test artefact: `jr build` resolves a declared `BUILD_OUTPUT` against the
# compiler process working directory (ADR-0122), which for `cargo test` is the
# crate directory. The test removes it, and this is the guard against a binary
# being committed again — one was.
/crates/jr-cli/named_by_script
